---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "The Second (and Final) JMIS Modification" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Scope of This Modification" },
        { id: "s4", label: "What Unmodified IFRS 9 Allows — the FVOCI No-Recycling Election for Equity Instruments" },
        { id: "s5", label: "THE MODIFICATION — Mandatory Eventual Recycling of All OCI Items" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Why the ASBJ Insisted on This Departure From IFRS" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Consistency With the Traditional Role of the Income Statement in Japanese Practice" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — an Equity Investment Sale Under JMIS vs Unmodified IFRS" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — a Loss on Disposal, Recycled Under JMIS" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a><a href="#s2">2. The Second (and Final) JMIS Modification</a><a href="#s3">3. Scope of This Modification</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. What Unmodified IFRS 9 Allows — the FVOCI No-Recycling Election for Equity Instruments</a><a href="#s5">5. THE MODIFICATION — Mandatory Eventual Recycling of All OCI Items</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Why the ASBJ Insisted on This Departure From IFRS</a><a href="#s7">7. Consistency With the Traditional Role of the Income Statement in Japanese Practice</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. Worked Example — an Equity Investment Sale Under JMIS vs Unmodified IFRS</a><a href="#s9">9. Worked Example — a Loss on Disposal, Recycled Under JMIS</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Disclosure Requirements</a><a href="#s11">11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</a>
      <a href="#s12">12. Relationship to IAS/IFRS</a><a href="#s13">13. Statement Mapping</a><a href="#s14">14. Related Standards</a><a href="#s15">15. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Ensuring cumulative comprehensive income eventually flows through profit or loss in full</div>
        <div class="principle">JMIS Modification Accounting Standard No. 2 requires that ALL items of OTHER COMPREHENSIVE INCOME (OCI) be EVENTUALLY reclassified ("RECYCLED") to PROFIT OR LOSS upon derecognition or settlement — CLOSING OFF a specific IFRS OPTION that would otherwise permit CERTAIN OCI gains/losses to bypass the Statement of Income PERMANENTLY, never touching reported profit or loss AT ALL.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>The Second (and Final) JMIS Modification</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Completing the pair, alongside the goodwill modification</div>
        <div class="principle">JMIS comprises IFRS Standards ENDORSED as issued by the IASB, SUBJECT to EXACTLY two ASBJ modifications — THIS one, addressing OTHER COMPREHENSIVE INCOME, and JMIS Modification No. 1 (Accounting for Goodwill — see the companion poster). TOGETHER, these TWO modifications represent the ENTIRE set of departures JMIS makes from UNMODIFIED international IFRS.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Scope of This Modification</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Companies electing to apply JMIS for consolidated statements</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">This modification applies to LISTED companies ELECTING JMIS for their CONSOLIDATED financial statements, specifically GOVERNING the SUBSEQUENT treatment of items initially recognised WITHIN Other Comprehensive Income.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>What Unmodified IFRS 9 Allows — the FVOCI No-Recycling Election for Equity Instruments</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">A genuine "parking" of gains/losses that never reach the income statement</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">UNDER unmodified IFRS 9, an entity may IRREVOCABLY ELECT to measure CERTAIN equity investments at FAIR VALUE THROUGH OTHER COMPREHENSIVE INCOME (FVOCI) — with a genuinely DISTINCTIVE feature: fair value CHANGES on these instruments are NEVER RECYCLED to profit or loss, EVEN upon SALE or disposal of the investment. The CUMULATIVE gain or loss SIMPLY remains PERMANENTLY within equity (OFTEN transferred directly to retained earnings on disposal) — meaning the ENTIRE economic gain or loss on such an investment can, in EFFECT, NEVER touch the Statement of Income AT ALL.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>THE MODIFICATION — Mandatory Eventual Recycling of All OCI Items</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Closing off the "permanent parking" option entirely</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">Under THIS JMIS modification, ALL items initially recognised WITHIN Other Comprehensive Income — INCLUDING fair value changes on EQUITY instruments that would OTHERWISE qualify for the unmodified IFRS 9 no-recycling ELECTION — must EVENTUALLY be RECLASSIFIED to PROFIT OR LOSS upon DERECOGNITION, DISPOSAL, or SETTLEMENT. The "PERMANENT PARKING" outcome unmodified IFRS 9 permits for FVOCI equity instruments is SIMPLY NOT AVAILABLE under JMIS — EVERY OCI item, WITHOUT exception, EVENTUALLY flows through the Statement of Income.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Why the ASBJ Insisted on This Departure From IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">The income statement should eventually capture all economic performance</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">The ASBJ has LONG held that the Statement of Income should, OVER TIME, capture the FULL economic PERFORMANCE of an entity's activities — a PHILOSOPHY reflected THROUGHOUT J-GAAP itself (see, for example, how the companion ASBJ Statement No. 10 poster describes "OTHER SECURITIES" fair value CHANGES eventually recycling through profit or loss on disposal). PERMITTING certain gains/losses to bypass the income statement PERMANENTLY — as unmodified IFRS 9's FVOCI equity election ALLOWS — was considered INCOMPATIBLE with this LONG-STANDING Japanese accounting PHILOSOPHY, prompting the ASBJ to CLOSE OFF this specific option within JMIS.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Consistency With the Traditional Role of the Income Statement in Japanese Practice</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A shared philosophy across J-GAAP and JMIS</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">This modification MIRRORS the SAME underlying philosophy already REFLECTED in J-GAAP's own OWN OCI-equivalent treatment (see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 25 and No. 10 posters) — CONSISTENT recycling of accumulated Valuation and Translation Adjustments through profit or loss upon a TRIGGERING event, RATHER than permitting SUCH items to bypass the Statement of Income INDEFINITELY.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — an Equity Investment Sale Under JMIS vs Unmodified IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">The same sale, two very different profit or loss outcomes</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Selling an FVOCI-elected equity investment at a gain</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company holds an equity investment, previously electing FVOCI measurement, with ¥60,000,000 of cumulative unrealised gains recognised within OCI. The company sells the investment during the year.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">Under <strong>JMIS</strong>, the ¥60,000,000 cumulative gain is <strong>RECLASSIFIED to PROFIT OR LOSS</strong> upon the sale — appearing as a gain in the CURRENT period's Statement of Income. Under <strong>UNMODIFIED IFRS 9</strong>, the SAME ¥60,000,000 would SIMPLY be TRANSFERRED directly WITHIN equity (e.g. to retained earnings), <strong>NEVER appearing</strong> in the Statement of Income AT ALL — a genuinely MATERIAL difference in REPORTED profit for the period of sale.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — a Loss on Disposal, Recycled Under JMIS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">The same principle applies symmetrically to losses</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Disposing of an investment with a cumulative unrealised loss</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company holds an FVOCI-elected equity investment with ¥25,000,000 of cumulative unrealised LOSSES recognised within OCI, and disposes of it during the year.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">Under JMIS, the ¥25,000,000 cumulative LOSS is <strong>RECLASSIFIED to PROFIT OR LOSS</strong> upon disposal — REDUCING reported profit for the period — CONSISTENT with the SAME mandatory recycling principle applying SYMMETRICALLY to both gains AND losses.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What this modification requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Amounts reclassified from OCI to profit or loss during the period, and the triggering events</span>
          <span>Cumulative OCI balances by component, prior to reclassification</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Identifying the correct triggering event for reclassification (disposal, derecognition, settlement)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Generally minimal — the reclassified amount is the cumulative balance already recognised within OCI</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — JMIS (as modified) vs unmodified IFRS 9</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">JMIS (Modification No. 2)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">Unmodified IFRS 9</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>FVOCI equity instrument no-recycling election</span><span>NOT available — all OCI eventually recycles</span><span>AVAILABLE — an irrevocable election permitting permanent non-recycling</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Other OCI components (e.g. FX translation, cash flow hedges)</span><span>Recycle upon the relevant triggering event</span><span>Also generally recycle — largely converged for these components</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">This modification's PRACTICAL impact is genuinely NARROW — it PRIMARILY affects the treatment of FVOCI-elected equity instruments specifically, since MOST other OCI components (foreign currency translation, cash flow hedges) ALREADY recycle under unmodified IFRS in the SAME way JMIS requires.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every OCI item lands under JMIS</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Disposal of an FVOCI-elected equity instrument</span><span><span class="badge bo">Net Assets/OCI</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Cumulative gain/loss reclassified to profit or loss</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 25</span><span>Presentation of Comprehensive Income — reflects the same recycling philosophy under J-GAAP itself</span></div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>JMIS Modification No. 1</span><span>The only other modification within the JMIS framework, addressing goodwill</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Recycling (reclassification)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">The transfer of a cumulative gain or loss previously recognised in OCI into profit or loss upon a triggering event such as disposal.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
          <div class="glossary-term">FVOCI no-recycling election (unmodified IFRS 9)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">An irrevocable IFRS 9 election permitting certain equity investments' fair value changes to never be reclassified to profit or loss, an option unavailable under JMIS.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP / JMIS terminology)</div>
      <div class="lrow">
        <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet / Statement of Financial Position
        <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement
        <span class="badge bo">Net Assets/OCI</span> Equity / Other Comprehensive Income
        <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets / Equity
        <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
